 at least two target words or phrases.","weight":0.2},{"criterion":"confidence","pass_description":"The learner attempts the task without abandoning it.","weight":0.15}],"scenario":"Maintain an eight-turn conversation.","task_type":"ai_conversation"},"pass_score":65},"content_safety":{"age_rating":"all_ages","sensitive_topics":[]},"duration_minutes":12,"lesson_id":"A1_STUDY_T04_L09","lesson_number":9,"mission":"Keep a simple conversation going.","objectives":["Use key words and phrases to keep a simple conversation going.","Understand a short beginner-level model conversation.","Complete a spoken mission with understandable English."],"rewards":{"bonus_condition":"Complete the final mission on the first attempt.","bonus_xp":25,"streak_credit":true,"xp":100},"scenario":"The learner uses English in a realistic study situation focused on friendship conversation.","target_language":{"grammar":[{"common_errors":["Using the wrong word order.","Leaving out a necessary verb or helper word."],"communicative_use":"Use this pattern to keep a simple conversation going.","examples":["Really?","Me too.","What about you?"],"pattern":"conversation extenders","point":"conversation extenders"}],"phrases":[{"audio_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_phrase_01","example":"Really?","formality":"neutral","phrase":"Really?","use_case":"Use this phrase to complete the lesson''s speaking mission."},{"audio_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_phrase_02","example":"Me too.","formality":"neutral","phrase":"Me too.","use_case":"Use this phrase to complete the lesson''s speaking mission."},{"audio_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_phrase_03","example":"What about you?","formality":"neutral","phrase":"What about you?","use_case":"Use this phrase to complete the lesson''s speaking mission."}],"pronunciation":[{"audio_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_pronunciation_01","common_error":"Speaking word by word with unclear stress.","focus":"Friendly rising and falling intonation in questions and greetings.","model":"Really?","tip":"Listen, pause, and repeat in one clear thought group."}],"vocabulary":[{"audio_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_vocab_01","example":"I use the word ''really'' in this lesson.","image_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_vocab_01","meaning":"A key word used in this lesson: really.","part_of_speech":"noun","simple_definition":"A simple A1 meaning for ''really''.","word":"really"},{"audio_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_vocab_02","example":"I use the word ''also'' in this lesson.","image_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_vocab_02","meaning":"A key word used in this lesson: also.","part_of_speech":"verb","simple_definition":"A simple A1 meaning for ''also''.","word":"also"},{"audio_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_vocab_03","example":"I use the word ''too'' in this lesson.","image_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_vocab_03","meaning":"A key word used in this lesson: too.","part_of_speech":"adjective","simple_definition":"A simple A1 meaning for ''too''.","word":"too"},{"audio_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_vocab_04","example":"I use the word ''what about'' in this lesson.","image_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_vocab_04","meaning":"A key word used in this lesson: what about.","part_of_speech":"adverb","simple_definition":"A simple A1 meaning for ''what about''.","word":"what about"},{"audio_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_vocab_05","example":"I use the word ''cool'' in this lesson.","image_key":"a1_study_t04_l09_vocab_05","meaning":"A key word used in this lesson: cool.","part_of_speech":"expression","simple_definition":"A simple A1 meaning for ''cool''.","word":"cool"}]},"title":"Friendship Conversation"}'::jsonb, NOW(), NOW())
